    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **46 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented rejection of a supplied `registrationDate` later than the server date with a 400 response, following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions.\n\nNew files:\n- **`ValidateOwnerRegistrationDate.java`** \u2014 a validation step reading `@Val Owner`; if the supplied `registrationDate` is after `LocalDate.now()`, throws the checked escalation. It runs *before* the default/weekend-adjust step, so the check is against the raw supplied value. An absent date (defaulted later) and any date on-or-before today are accepted.\n- **`FutureRegistrationDateException.java`** \u2014 checked exception (`extends Exception`).\n- **`FutureRegistrationDateExceptionHandler.java`** \u2014 responds `400 BAD_REQUEST` with `{\"errors\":[\"registrationDate\"]}`, mirroring the existing postcode handler.\n- **`...FutureRegistrationDateException.yml`** \u2014 escalation wiring under `officefloor/escalation/`.\n\nEdited:\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted a `validateRegistrationDate` step (with `govern: [ transaction ]`) between `household-size` and the existing `registrationDate` default step.\n\nVerification:\n- `Cp33Tests` (new, future date `2999-01-01` \u2192 400) passes.\n- Regression checks pass: `Cp07` (supplied past weekend date rolls to Monday), `Cp20` (default date is a business day), `Cp14`/`Cp21` (registrationDate in response/audit), and the full 46-test suite.",
